    <string name="signal_about_title">Bit-perfect or processed?</string>
    <string name="signal_about_bitperfect">Bit-perfect: HomeFi hands the song to Android exactly as it is in the file, sample for sample. No equalizer, no loudness change, no rate conversion.</string>
    <string name="signal_about_resampled">Resampled: HomeFi leaves the samples alone, but the output runs at another sample rate, so Android converts them on the way.</string>
    <string name="signal_about_processed">Processed: something changes the samples on the way (the equalizer, a taste layer or even loudness). It can sound better on your headphones; it just is no longer the untouched file.</string>
    <string name="signal_about_android">On Android the system mixer and volume sit between every app and the output, so bit-perfect here means HomeFi itself changes nothing.</string>
